## The following text has been annotated for parts of speech by students at NTU Singapore as part of a class project in AY 2025-26.
## Verses are extracted from the taggedPBC. Annotations have been developed with a combination of manual and automated approaches, with reference to existing literature and (where possible) native speakers.
## ISO 639-3: dis, Language: Dimasa, Number of verses: 21
## References: Burling, R. (2003). NORTHEASTERN INDIA¹. The Sino-Tibetan Languages, 3, 169. ; Evans, J. P., & Langthasa, D. (2024). Dimasa language: structure and texts. Institute of Linguistics, Academia Sinica. ; Jacquesson, F. (2008). Discovering Boro-Garo History of an analytical and descriptive linguistic category. European bulletin of Himalayan research, 32, 14-49.

